			"notes": "# v 1.0.0 Changelogs\n\n## Added Skin Flicker Module\n\n* This is the coolest module ever. It toggless on and off layers of your skin to make an effect that's cool asf. It's very customizable, you can choose between different modes, directions, delays, randomize the delays, the layers, or choose which layers you want to be flickered and which ones you don't.\n* This module as far as I know, at this very moment is only available for paid clients, such as mio client, which in my opinion is a waste ef money. This means I assume I'm the first one releasing the code as open source for this feature. I hope everyone will use this module and realize that paid clients suck. In fact I think my module adds more customization options than any paid client. Open source FTW!\n\n![Skin Flicker](https://github.com/Plumbiller/PlumbillerPublic/blob/main/src/main/resources/assets/publicaddon/docs_assets/SkinFlicker-Plumbiller.gif)\n\n**Disclaimer:** If your skin does not have layers (hat, jacket, pants, etc.) this module will do nothing. The cool effect you an see in the gif and in my skin in-game is because the top layers of my skin are responsible for that glitch effect.\n\n# Added support for multi versions\nNow supporting versions 1.21.4, 1.21.5, 1.21.6, 1.21.7, 1.21.8, 1.21.10 and 1.21.11 is easier than ever.\n* Added [Multi version compatibility](https://github.com/Plumbiller/PlumbillerPublic/blob/main/src/main/java/com/Plumbiller/publicaddon/util/MultiVersionCompat.java). Since different Minecraft versions have different obfuscated names or API changes (e.g., getWorld vs getEntityWorld), this project uses a utility class com.Plumbiller.publicaddon.util.MultiVersionCompat. This class uses reflection to dynamically find the correct method at runtime, ensuring the same JAR works (logic-wise) for all versions. This means I no longer need different branches for different minecraft versions, because all versions are supported by the exact same code, which makes my life 7 times easier. Sice those extra branches are no longer needed I removed them.\n* Custom gradlew tasks to build the mod. Since the same code now supports all 7 different versions, to make everything easier for me and for users, I added custom gradlew tasks such as buildAll, which builds all supported versions of my addon in one go, or build_v(mc version) which builds the mod for the specified version.\n\n_**Examples**_\n```powershell\n.\\gradlew buildAll\n```\n```powershell\n.\\gradlew build_v1.21.11\n```\n```powershell\n.\\gradlew build_v1.21.4\n```\nFor more information about multi version compatibility and how to build the mod, you can read the [MULTIVERSION documentation](https://github.com/Plumbiller/PlumbillerPublic/blob/main/MULTIVERSION.md).\n\n## Modified the in game docs menu\n* The custom menu I made to display all the addon information has been completely changed, it's now is based on meteor GUIs, meaning the style, theme, colors, etc. Will be consistent with your meteor settings. This makes the menu more visually pleasing and consistent with meteor aesthetics. It also supports colored text to make it easier fot the user to read.\n* Also the coolest thing is that you can see the config of each module integrated in the documentation. This means the user is able to read the documentation about the features of my mod while seeing and tweaking their configs in real time, which I hope makes the documentation easier to understand and more interactive.\n<img width=\"1919\" height=\"1079\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cfb4834d-1c4a-4796-b469-fb543cd98189\" />\n<img width=\"1919\" height=\"1079\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6cc4ff3e-5508-4f13-95ea-1e0a1db7d6b3\" />\n<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1080\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/870bdef4-5a72-459a-81da-16aa4475ecbb\" />\n\n# Added BetterTabFix module\n* Removed the old TabFix module from version 0.0.5.\n\n..."
		},
