			"notes": "I'm releasing a 1.21.4 version of the module too, even though the main version that will be supported at the moment and the near future is 1.21.7. I don't know if I will keep supporting 1.21.4 minecraft version from now on, depends on how annoying it is.\n**Changelog:**\n- Added a PlumbillerPublic button in the minecraft title screen right when your game launches, where you can see in game the docs of the mod.\n- Updated README.md to display these docs.\n- Added RestrictedAreas feature that includes a module and commands. You can create restricted areas in your client which are saved **locally** in a .json archive inside your \"PlumbillerAddon\" directory in your minecraft installation folder. It's highly configurable and visual. This allows you to create areas in your world/server where specific players are authorized to teleport inside. You can automatically manage the teleport requests (accept, deny and toggle) if you want. More information about restricted areas in the docs.\n- Enhanced AutoRename module to correct minor bugs."
